.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-VERSION 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-version
.Nd print the version of noqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis version
.Op Fl -check
.Nm noqtis
.Fl V | Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis version
prints
.Dl noqtis <major>.<minor>.<patch>
the version of the library the tool runs on, as
.Fn nqver
returns it
.Pq Xr nqerr 3 .
.Pp
With
.Fl -check
it asks instead whether a newer release exists, and prints either that
this version is up to date or the newer version and the address of its
release.
The question is the request for the page of the latest release, with a
limit of ten seconds; nothing else is sent.
.Pp
The other commands say the same in one line on standard error, after
their work and with status 0, when a newer release exists: see
.Ev NOQTIS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK
in
.Xr noqtis 1 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0; 1 when
.Fl -check
cannot ask (no network, or nothing to ask with); 2 on a usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis version | cut -d' ' -f1
noqtis
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr nqerr 3
